    "title": "Brazil vs France Lineups, Live Streams, Cable, How & Where to Watch In the USA",
    "text": "The March international break will feature a highly anticipated friendly between two nations that are favorites to win the 2026 World Cup: Brazil and France.Both teams have elite attacking players, and the two national teams qualified for the World Cup last year through their respective World Cup qualifiers in their respective regions or confederations.AdvertisementBrazil qualified for the 2026 World Cup by finishing fifth with 28 points after 18 CONMEBOL World Cup qualifying matches played.Brazil has played four friendlies after securing its spot in the World Cup. Their previous friendly was Nov. 18, 2025, against Tunisia. That match finished 1-1; Estevao was the goalscorer for Brazil.France qualified for the 2026 World Cup by finishing first in Group D of the UEFA World Cup qualifiers. France was in Group D with Ukraine, Iceland and Azerbaijan.AdvertisementFrance finished first with 16 points on a record of five wins and one draw. France won all of its home games in France.In its previous match, France beat Azerbaijan 3-1 away from home on goals from Jean-Philippe Mateta, Maghnes Akliouche and an own goal of Shahrudin Mahammadaliyev.Kylian Mbappe of France celebrates scoring his team's first goal with teammates from the penalty spot during the FIFA World Cup 2026 qualifier match between France and Ukraine at Parc des Princes on November 13, 2025 in Paris, France. (Photo by Franco Arland/Getty Images)Photo by Franco Arland/Getty Images (Photo by Franco Arland&sol;Getty Images)Brazil and France last played each other in 2015. It was a friendly on March 26, 2015, that was won by Brazil 3-1.Official Lineups and Injuries for Brazil and FranceBrazilGoalkeeper: EdersonDefenders: Douglas Santos, Leo Pereira, Gleison Bremer, WesleyMidfielders: Gabriel Martinelli, Andrey Santos, Casemiro, RaphinhaForwards: Vinicius Junior, Matheus CunhaAdvertisementBRASIL DEFINIDO! 🇧🇷Confira os 11 nomes escalados pelo Mister para enfrentar a França nesta quinta (26), às 17h (Brasília).📺 TV GLOBO / SporTV / GE TV🏟️ GILETTE STADIUMVAMOS JUNTOS, VAMOS BRASIL! 🫵 pic.twitter.com/L4OO0Nl8HW— brasil (@CBF_Futebol) March 26, 2026Injuries: Alisson Becker, Gabriel, Alex Sandro, MarquinhosFranceGoalkeeper: Mike MaignanDefenders: Theo Hernandez, Dayot Upamecano, Ibrahima Konate, Malo GustoMidfielders: Adrien Rabiot, Aurelien TchouameniForwards: Hugo Ekitike, Kylian Mbappe, Ousmane Dembele, Michael OliseInjuries: William Saliba, Manu KoneBrazil and France will kick off at 4 p.m. ET/ 1 p.m. PT in the United States. The match will kick off at 4 p.m. local time at Gillette Stadium in Foxborough, Massachusetts, in the United States.Gillette Stadium will be one of the sites for 2026 World Cup games this summer.The match will be available to watch across select TV channels and streaming services in the United States and in other countries.AdvertisementESPN Unlimited (USA)ESPN Deportes (USA)ESPN 2 (USA)Fubo Sports (USA)TF1 (France)TV GLOBO / SporTV / GE TV (Brazil)This story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 26, 2026, where it first appeared in the Soccer section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
